%I A401113 #17 Oct 21 2026 22:26:41
%S A401113 2,2082927199,2082927221,2082927239,2082927281,2082927299,2082928481,
%T A401113 2082928501,2082928609,2082928739,2082928759,2082929041,2082929599,
%U A401113 2082929801,2082929899,2082930061,2082930079,2082935201,2082935209,2082953029,2082953231,2082953281
%N A401113 Primes p at which the running sum Sum_{q prime <= p} Kronecker(5,q) sets a new record high.
%C A401113 a(1) = 2 (sum = -1), a(2) = 2082927199 (the sum first returns to 0 after two billion integers), a(3) = 2082927221 (the first negative term of A321857).
%C A401113 The sum first reaches +263 at a(265) = 15071146729 (the records are exactly the consecutive integers -1, 0, 1, 2, ...).
%C A401113 The 265 terms below 10^11 lie in two short clusters of excursions: around 2.083*10^9 and between 1.461*10^10 and 1.508*10^10.
%C A401113 a(n) is the smallest prime p such that Sum_{q prime <= p} Kronecker(5,q) = n-2.
%D A401113 Andrew Granville and Greg Martin, Prime number races, Amer. Math. Monthly, 113 (2006) 1-33.
%H A401113 Ved Prakash Pandey, <a href="/A401113/b401113.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..859</a>
%H A401113 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%e A401113 a(3) = 2082927221: the sum first reaches 1 at this prime (2082927221 is the first negative term of A321857, which is the negated sum).
%o A401113 (PARI) my(s=0, r=-2); forprime(p=2, 2*10^10, s += kronecker(5, p); if (s > r, r = s; print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A401113 Cf. A321857 (negated sum), A326615, A392295, A392296, A392297, A392298, A392299, A080891.
%K A401113 nonn,new
%O A401113 1,1
%A A401113 _Ved Prakash Pandey_, Oct 15 2026
